## Purpose of Function:                                                             #
## HTTPS-triggered Azure Function that exposes ONE endpoint with TWO modes,         #
## selected by the 'agent' field in the request:                                    #
##      1. agent = 'detect'    -> returns ONLY the detected language of 'message'   #
##         [LLM based via Azure OpenAI; py3langid offline detector as fallback].    #
##      2. agent = 'translate' -> translates 'message' into the target 'lang' using #
##         the same Azure OpenAI model.                                             #
##                                                                                  #
## Request contract [query string OR JSON body]:                                    #
##      agent    : 'detect' | 'translate'                    [required]             #
##      message  : text to detect / translate                [required]             #
##      lang     : target language for 'translate'         [required for translate] #
##                 [ISO code 'ja', alias 'jp' or name 'Japanese']                   #
##                                                                                  #
##      !! 'agent' IS ONLY A FIELD NAME. It is the mode selector in the caller's    #
##         payload and NOTHING in this module resolves, hosts or invokes an AI      #
##         agent. The name is frozen because live callers and the Postman suite     #
##         send it; the code reads it via extract_llm_mode[] into 'llm_mode'.       #
##         Rename it to 'mode' only alongside a coordinated caller update.          #
##                                                                                  #
## How a request flows:                                                             #
##      main[] -> extract_llm_mode[] -> validate -> LlmService -> ONE HTTPS POST to #
##      the Azure OpenAI /chat/completions endpoint -> JSON response.               #
##      'detect' can short-circuit to ZERO LLM calls on a rejected script, and      #
##      degrades to the offline py3langid engine if the model is unreachable.       #
##      'translate' has no offline path: it succeeds, 400s, or 502s.                #
##                                                                                  #
## Performance note [WHY the model is called DIRECTLY]:                             #
##      The first cut went through the Foundry Agents API, resolving a deployment   #
##      BY NAME over the Responses API. That cost TWO upstream round-trips per      #
##      request plus a server-side lookup on every single call, and it dominated    #
##      end-to-end latency. The system prompt now lives in THIS file                #
##      [LLM_SYSTEM_PROMPT] and the model is called directly over Chat              #
##      Completions: ONE round-trip, no name resolution, no conversation object.    #
##      The request/response contract is unchanged - callers do not change.         #
##                                                                                  #
## Model note:                                                                      #
##      Default deployment is 'gpt-5-mini' [model version 2025-08-07], a REASONING  #
##      model. It takes 'max_completion_tokens' [not 'max_tokens'], rejects any     #
##      non-default 'temperature', and supports 'reasoning_effort' - set to         #
##      'minimal' here because both modes are short mechanical tasks. Reasoning     #
##      tokens are billed against the output ceiling, which is why the detect cap   #
##      is 512 rather than 8. If the deployment is ever swapped to a gpt-4o family  #
##      model, _chat detects the rejected parameters and flips dialect once.        #
##                                                                                  #
## Production hardening applied:                                                    #
##      - LLM client + credential are built ONCE and reused across requests.        #
##      - Per-call timeout + automatic retries on the LLM calls.                    #
##      - Bounded input length [MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS] to protect cost / prevent abuse. #
##      - Bounded OUTPUT ceiling + minimal reasoning effort so replies stay fast.   #
##      - Only the first DETECT_SAMPLE_CHARS characters are sent for detection.     #
##      - No internal exception detail leaked to callers; full detail is logged.    #
##      - correlation_id on EVERY response and injected into EVERY log record.      #
##      - Structured logs [extra=...] with latency + engine ['foundry' | 'offline'].#
##                                                                                  #
## Authentication:                                                                  #
##      The Azure OpenAI endpoint is reached with Microsoft Entra ID; no API keys   #
##      are used or stored. The Function App's Managed Identity MUST live in the    #
##      SAME tenant as the Azure OpenAI / Foundry resource and hold the             #
##      'Cognitive Services OpenAI User' role [or 'Azure AI User'] on it.           #
##      Token scope: https://cognitiveservices.azure.com/.default                   #
##                                                                                  #
## Note:-                                                                           #
##      - This module is self contained [no local project imports]; the helpers     #
##        below play the same role the shared utils/app_config files play elsewhere.#
##          - load_config:- Builds the configuration [endpoints, deployment, env]   #
##                          from App Settings with safe defaults.                   #
##          - json_response:- This is used to standardise the response.             #
##          - error_response:- Standard error envelope carrying the correlation id. #
##          - get_default_credential:- To validate using managed identity.          #
##          - sanitize_correlation_id:- Guards against log injection via headers.   #
##          - extract_llm_mode / extract_message / extract_lang:- Read and          #
##            validate the input from the caller [query string or JSON body].       #
##      - LanguageDetector [py3langid] is the OFFLINE fallback engine so the        #
##        'detect' mode keeps working even when the LLM cannot be reached.          #
##      - LlmService is the wrapper used for BOTH detection and translation;        #
##        it issues exactly ONE Chat Completions call per request.                  #
##      - Tunable App Settings [all optional, safe defaults in code]:               #
##        AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT, AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT,                           #
##        AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION, ENVIRONMENT, MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS,                 #
##        LLM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS, LLM_MAX_RETRIES, LLM_PARAM_STYLE,                    #
##        LLM_REASONING_EFFORT, LLM_TEMPERATURE, DETECT_MAX_TOKENS,                 #
##        TRANSLATE_MAX_TOKENS, DETECT_SAMPLE_CHARS, LOG_LEVEL.                     #
##      - NO LONGER READ [delete these two App Settings from the Function App]:     #
##        FOUNDRY_ENDPOINT, FOUNDRY_AGENT_NAME. Nothing in this module looks them   #
##        up any more; leaving them in place is harmless but misleading.            #
##        FOUNDRY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS / FOUNDRY_MAX_RETRIES ARE still honoured, as a    #
##        fallback for the LLM_* names, so existing tuning keeps working.           #
